Subject: [PATCH v5 0/7] ARM: Exynos: Enable device tree support for MCT
 controller
Message-ID: <1361175225-19282-1-git-send-email-thomas.abraham@linaro.org>
To: linux-arm-kernel@lists.infradead.org
List-Id: linux-arm-kernel.lists.infradead.org

Changes since v4:
- Rebased to 3.8-rc7
- Updated the MCT controller device nodes to list all the four global timer
  interrupts generated by the MCT controller.

Changes since v3:
- Based on Stephen Warren's CONFIG_CLKSRC_OF patches (merged from arm-soc
  'timer/cleanup' branch).
- Moved the mct driver from mach-exynos to drivers/clocksource as suggested
  by Olof.

Changes since v2:
- Rebased to linux 3.8-rc1

Changes since v1:
- Includes changes suggested by Sylwester Nawrocki <sylvester.nawrocki@gmail.com>

This patch series adds device tree support for Exynos4/5 MCT controller and
moves the MCT driver from mach-exynos to drivers/clocksource. This has been
tested on Exynos4210 based Origen board, Exynos4412 based Origen board and
Exynos5250 based SMDK board.
